NOT RUN (the person who wrote the sheet)
  - PARTLY SEEN: the fvg_oside family's unseen months (2025-07 on) were read three times on 15-minute bars (the 1-a-day sibling's walk-forward, the lane's no-cap walk-forward, the Desk walk-forward) and again in cl_fvg_oside_15_mid_r1_t2_gap0p1's walk-forward. This 5-minute sheet with a VWAP side makes different trades on the same months: its walk-forward is not fully blind.
  - THE VWAP: the engine's session VWAP, which restarts at each session pass start (09:30, 11:00 and 13:30 ET), not one VWAP from 09:30; the gate reads (close - VWAP) / sigma at the gap's 5-minute close (closed bars only): above 0 for a long, below 0 for a short. The gate is checked when the order is placed or moved.
  - THE SIDE vs the 09:30 open is read on each 5-minute close, not tick by tick.
  - THE STOP: 3 x the mean true range of the 14 newest completed 1-minute bars at the gap's close, measured from the near edge, without the engine's 0.25 x tf-ATR floor (two ticks only).
  - ONE INSTANCE 09:30-15:58: the cap of 3 is a DAY cap and one position at a time holds all day; an unfilled order is cancelled at 15:00.
  - COSTS AND FILLS: the engine's own (1 tick of slippage, $4 a round turn, tick replay, strict limit fills).
  - THE TEST DAYS (2025-07-01 on) ARE NOT READ by this sheet: build days only.
  - FLAT: every trade is flat by 15:58 ET (13:13 on half days).

ALSO TRUE OF THE RUN (the lane)
  - ONE INSTANCE FOR THE DAY (nyam, mid, pm are one window, entries 10:30-15:30, flat 15:58): the cap of 3 trades is a DAY cap, one position at a time holds for the whole day, and the family's loss stop counts over the day (none). The random control and the reads still go pass by pass (nyam, mid, pm), matched by day.
  - Every trade is flat by 15:58 ET (13:13 on an equity half day); no entry in the last 5 minutes of a pass.
  - Costs: $4.00 a round turn and 1 tick of slippage on market and stop fills, 1 contract (the engine's own).
  - The stop is the family's structure level of each entry (its size differs from trade to trade; the engine never puts it closer than two ticks or 0.25 ATR); `stop_val` is not used.

HONEST LIMITS
  - One video's rule, read on the build days (2021-09-22 .. 2025-06-30): in-sample.
  - The family's settings and the exits are the video's own: nothing was tuned, searched or picked.
  - The neighbours are shown to see how fragile the rule is; they are not alternatives to choose from.
  - The unseen days (2025-07-01 on) were not read: a person has to ask for that, and it is read once.
  - The random entries are the pipeline's own (any bar of the session pass, matched by day and pass): they do not wait for the family's entry window.
